WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.476
Today is September 23, 2026.

3
00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:12.451
Overnight, the Nasdaq digested its sharp rally on Meta's Muse launch.

4
00:00:12.451 --> 00:00:16.618
The S and P five hundred posted only marginal gains.

5
00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:19.326
The Dow tracked essentially flat.

6
00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:22.782
Volume stayed thin despite index highs.

7
00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:26.434
That is the single most important read in today's tape.

8
00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.750
The market is not chasing.

9
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.822
It is consolidating.

10
00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:34.388
Investment grade credit spreads widened overnight.

11
00:00:34.388 --> 00:00:37.880
The bond market is still pricing macro risk.

12
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.197
The stock market is not.

13
00:00:40.197 --> 00:00:42.488
That divergence matters.

14
00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:46.716
On the energy side, Brent slid below one hundred dollars.

15
00:00:46.716 --> 00:00:49.939
The Saudi East West pipeline restarted.

16
00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:53.665
Yanbu port is resuming crude exports this week.

17
00:00:53.665 --> 00:00:57.525
Washington and Tehran both signaled willingness to talk.

18
00:00:57.525 --> 00:01:01.177
Trump hinted at a back channel meeting during the U N run.

19
00:01:01.177 --> 00:01:03.652
None of that is a signed deal.

20
00:01:03.652 --> 00:01:06.238
The Houthi threat is not gone.

21
00:01:06.238 --> 00:01:09.265
But the oil tailwind is being priced in.

22
00:01:09.265 --> 00:01:12.035
It will not drive another leg higher.

23
00:01:12.035 --> 00:01:18.885
On the policy front, Treasury Secretary Bessent confirmed a bilateral AI dialogue framework with Beijing.

24
00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:23.420
Markets are reading that as marginal easing on chip export controls.

25
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.140
Trump also dropped a strange one.

26
00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:31.091
Government documents will now use the term Superintelligence instead of AI.

27
00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:34.988
He opposes any global mandatory AI restriction.

28
00:01:34.988 --> 00:01:37.868
The regulatory overhang is lightening.

29
00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:39.927
At least domestically.

30
00:01:39.927 --> 00:01:44.988
Now let's connect that macro liquidity picture to where capital is actually flowing.

31
00:01:44.988 --> 00:01:49.167
The AI agent narrative is reshaping the hardware stack.

32
00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:52.562
This is not a GPU-only story anymore.

33
00:01:52.562 --> 00:01:57.145
An AI agent does not generate one text response and stop.

34
00:01:57.145 --> 00:01:59.939
It sits in the background for hours.

35
00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:03.383
It loops through multi step task orchestration.

36
00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:06.103
It pulls local data repeatedly.

37
00:02:06.103 --> 00:02:08.775
It hammers service APIs.

38
00:02:08.775 --> 00:02:11.692
It runs parallel workflow logic.

39
00:02:11.692 --> 00:02:16.128
That sustained multi thread scheduling load is a CPU problem.

40
00:02:16.128 --> 00:02:24.645
Jefferies projects global server CPU shipments climbing from twenty nine million units in twenty twenty five to seventy five million by twenty thirty.

41
00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:28.542
The substrate and packaging market scales in lockstep.

42
00:02:28.542 --> 00:02:31.422
The tape confirmed it on the twenty first.

43
00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:34.216
ARM ripped over fifteen percent.

44
00:02:34.216 --> 00:02:36.434
Intel jumped twelve.

45
00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:42.108
AMD surged nearly ten percent and crossed the one trillion dollar market cap mark.

46
00:02:42.108 --> 00:02:46.447
That is a structural demand shift, not a one day rotation.

47
00:02:46.447 --> 00:02:49.351
GPU remains the foundation.

48
00:02:49.351 --> 00:02:52.574
But a second compute axis is now live.

49
00:02:52.574 --> 00:02:55.613
The agent war is also a data war.

50
00:02:55.613 --> 00:03:01.581
Unlike chatbots where model parameters can be matched, agents compete on user behavior data.

51
00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:05.050
They compete on cross ecosystem connectivity.

52
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.542
They compete on long term habit accumulation.

53
00:03:08.542 --> 00:03:11.263
Switching costs are enormous.

54
00:03:11.263 --> 00:03:14.939
OpenAI is still anchored in dialogue models.

55
00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:17.954
Its consumer agent rollout is lagging.

56
00:03:17.954 --> 00:03:20.871
Meta is out ahead on the product front.

57
00:03:20.871 --> 00:03:24.375
That is where we get to the stock that defined this week.

58
00:03:24.375 --> 00:03:29.510
Meta's Muse hit number one on the U S App Store free chart within two weeks.

59
00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:33.812
It beat every prior Meta AI product on growth velocity.

60
00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:37.170
The product is fundamentally different from a chatbot.

61
00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.871
It proactively executes multi step tasks.

62
00:03:40.871 --> 00:03:43.309
It remembers your preferences.

63
00:03:43.309 --> 00:03:46.704
It auto compares prices and places orders.

64
00:03:46.704 --> 00:03:49.461
It books restaurants and hotels.

65
00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:52.268
It manages your Gmail inbox.

66
00:03:52.268 --> 00:03:54.633
It orchestrates your calendar.

67
00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:57.402
It links Spotify and Instagram.

68
00:03:57.402 --> 00:04:00.981
It cancels subscriptions and recovers refunds.

69
00:04:00.981 --> 00:04:04.277
It filters the best dealer quotes on a car.

70
00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:09.768
The revenue model is subscription plus e commerce commission plus service revenue share.

71
00:04:09.768 --> 00:04:14.130
Free tier, twenty dollar premium, one hundred dollar tier.

72
00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.635
Wall Street is re-rating the stock on that basis.

73
00:04:17.635 --> 00:04:22.317
Wells Fargo lifted its target from six forty to seven ninety six.

74
00:04:22.317 --> 00:04:24.743
The core thesis is this.

75
00:04:24.743 --> 00:04:28.947
Meta has poured nearly two hundred billion dollars into AI.

76
00:04:28.947 --> 00:04:33.591
For the first time, that spend produced a product users will pay for.

77
00:04:33.591 --> 00:04:36.826
The cost center is becoming a revenue engine.

78
00:04:36.826 --> 00:04:40.662
Every additional user interaction deepens the data moat.

79
00:04:40.662 --> 00:04:43.812
More usage means better personalization.

80
00:04:43.812 --> 00:04:47.182
Better personalization means higher retention.

81
00:04:47.182 --> 00:04:49.878
Higher retention means more data.

82
00:04:49.878 --> 00:04:52.562
That flywheel is the bull case.

83
00:04:52.562 --> 00:04:55.625
But the bear case is real and specific.

84
00:04:55.625 --> 00:05:00.760
Amazon has already banned Muse from executing auto checkout on its platform.

85
00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:03.113
The reason is straightforward.

86
00:05:03.113 --> 00:05:06.042
Muse bypasses the recommendation

87
00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:07.744
algorithm.

88
00:05:07.694 --> 00:05:10.819
It scrapes the lowest price across the web.

89
00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:15.611
That directly attacks Amazon's ad auction and traffic pricing power.

90
00:05:15.611 --> 00:05:18.809
China already played this exact script.

91
00:05:18.809 --> 00:05:24.140
Domestic auto operation AI assistants got blocked by every major platform.

92
00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:28.944
Meta's own ecosystem, Facebook and Instagram, is safe.

93
00:05:28.944 --> 00:05:33.577
Native APIs, full compliance, long term iteration.

94
00:05:33.577 --> 00:05:38.724
But the cross platform, unrestricted agent narrative will face repeated friction.

95
00:05:38.724 --> 00:05:41.603
More platforms will follow Amazon.

96
00:05:41.603 --> 00:05:45.660
The market's high expectations need a haircut on that dimension.

97
00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.755
Muse will not fail.

98
00:05:47.755 --> 00:05:50.746
The Meta ecosystem loop is durable.

99
00:05:50.746 --> 00:05:54.778
But the grand unified agent story is going to get chipped away.

100
00:05:54.778 --> 00:05:58.417
That is the risk to monitor into the next two quarters.

101
00:05:58.417 --> 00:06:00.513
Now the second name.

102
00:06:00.513 --> 00:06:02.118
Nvidia.

103
00:06:02.118 --> 00:06:07.853
Jensen Huang called the company the only global growth value stock at the Goldman tech conference.

104
00:06:07.853 --> 00:06:10.733
The data does not agree with that framing.

105
00:06:10.733 --> 00:06:15.304
Forward earnings multiple has compressed to roughly seventeen times.

106
00:06:15.304 --> 00:06:17.461
That is a decade low.

107
00:06:17.461 --> 00:06:20.280
Four pressures are capping the re rating.

108
00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.437
First, margin.

109
00:06:22.437 --> 00:06:26.849
The company has guided gross margin down from seventy five percent.

110
00:06:26.849 --> 00:06:30.893
Quarter four likely lands at seventy one to seventy two.

111
00:06:30.893 --> 00:06:35.329
Long term equilibrium settles at seventy two to seventy three.

112
00:06:35.329 --> 00:06:38.883
Storage chip costs are the primary squeeze.

113
00:06:38.883 --> 00:06:42.228
Second, hyperscaler custom silicon.

114
00:06:42.228 --> 00:06:48.699
Morgan Stanley and JPMorgan both flag that the CPU and custom ASIC share gap is narrowing.

115
00:06:48.699 --> 00:06:51.787
The single vendor dependency is eroding.

116
00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:54.802
Third, capex sustainability.

117
00:06:54.802 --> 00:07:00.819
If the big cloud players pause their build out, Nvidia's revenue curve flattens immediately.

118
00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:03.417
Funds are front running that risk.

119
00:07:03.417 --> 00:07:06.273
Fourth, the base is enormous.

120
00:07:06.273 --> 00:07:10.059
Doubling from here requires a blowout fundamental print.

121
00:07:10.059 --> 00:07:12.780
A good quarter is no longer enough.

122
00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.684
The valuation floor looks soft.

123
00:07:15.684 --> 00:07:19.851
But the structural demand from agents and inference is still building.

124
00:07:19.851 --> 00:07:24.765
This is a stock where the story is intact but the multiple has lost its premium.

125
00:07:24.765 --> 00:07:29.827
Watch for any hyperscaler guidance that hints at reduced Nvidia allocation.

126
00:07:29.827 --> 00:07:32.228
That is the trigger to watch.

127
00:07:32.228 --> 00:07:34.030
The third name.

128
00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.635
AMD.

129
00:07:35.635 --> 00:07:38.577
One trillion dollars of market cap.

130
00:07:38.577 --> 00:07:41.922
That number was unthinkable eighteen months ago.

131
00:07:41.922 --> 00:07:44.471
The driver is not GPU.

132
00:07:44.471 --> 00:07:48.515
It is the CPU re acceleration I described earlier.

133
00:07:48.515 --> 00:07:53.099
AI agents are a sustained scheduling and orchestration workload.

134
00:07:53.099 --> 00:07:57.290
That is squarely in AMD's server processor sweet spot.

135
00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:00.219
The competitive dynamic has shifted.

136
00:08:00.219 --> 00:08:04.287
Intel is no longer the only x86 alternative.

137
00:08:04.287 --> 00:08:08.797
AMD is capturing the share that was previously Intel's default.

138
00:08:08.797 --> 00:08:13.478
The one trillion mark signals institutional re allocation is complete.

139
00:08:13.478 --> 00:08:18.711
The next leg depends on whether the agent build out accelerates into twenty twenty seven.

140
00:08:18.711 --> 00:08:21.101
The risk is concentration.

141
00:08:21.101 --> 00:08:28.025
If one or two hyperscalers lock in a custom silicon roadmap, the CPU growth narrative gets a headwind.

142
00:08:28.025 --> 00:08:34.153
But the Jefferies seventy five million unit projection by twenty thirty is the floor, not the ceiling.

143
00:08:34.153 --> 00:08:37.510
One final macro note before we close.

144
00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:40.378
Next week, Micron reports.

145
00:08:40.378 --> 00:08:45.415
That is the single most important data point for the entire AI hardware trade.

146
00:08:45.415 --> 00:08:51.113
The market is waiting for Micron to confirm that memory and storage demand is still expanding.

147
00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:56.211
If the numbers validate the capex cycle, the consolidation breaks higher.

148
00:08:56.211 --> 00:09:01.653
If they disappoint, the thin volume we saw overnight turns into a real correction.

149
00:09:01.653 --> 00:09:04.189
That is the binary to watch.

150
00:09:04.189 --> 00:09:07.829
Position sizing matters more than direction this week.

151
00:09:07.829 --> 00:09:09.765
Keep stops tight.

152
00:09:09.765 --> 00:09:12.461
Do not average into a gap down.

153
00:09:12.461 --> 00:09:17.106
The credit spread divergence tells you the bond market is not convinced yet.

154
00:09:17.106 --> 00:09:18.822
Respect that.

155
00:09:18.822 --> 00:09:22.829
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

156
00:09:22.829 --> 00:09:26.996
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
